.TH UI 2
.SH NAME
uiopen, uinew, uictl, uiset, uievent, uiclose \- a client of ui(4)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <u.h>
.br
.B #include <libc.h>
.br
.B #include <ui.h>
.PP
.ta \w'\fLUi* 'u
.B
Ui*	uiopen(char *srv, char *mtpt)
.PP
.B
Ui*	uinew(char *title, char *mtpt)
.PP
.B
int	uictl(Ui *u, char *fmt, ...)
.PP
.B
int	uiset(Ui *u, char *id, char *key, char *value)
.PP
.B
int	uievent(Ui *u, Uievent *e)
.PP
.B
void	uiclose(Ui *u)
.SH DESCRIPTION
These routines are a thin layer over the files of
.IR ui (4):
a window of widgets that a program describes in
.BR ctl 's
language and whose events it reads from
.BR event .
Everything they do can be done with
.IR open (2),
.IR read (2)
and
.IR write (2)
on the files as well.
.PP
.I Uiopen
mounts
.BI /srv/ srv\fR,
the files of a running
.IR ui ,
on
.I mtpt
(default
.BR /mnt/ui )
and opens its
.B ctl
and
.BR event .
.I Uinew
starts
.B /bin/ui
in a new window of
.IR rio (1)
or
.IR wsys (4)
.RB ( window
in
.IR rio (1)),
waits up to ten seconds for its files and opens them as
.I uiopen
does; a
.I title
not nil is the window's.
.PP
.I Uictl
writes a transaction: the text
.I fmt
makes
.RI ( print (2)),
its lines applied all or none.
It returns 0, or \-1 with the error
.I ui
gave (which names the line).
.I Uiset
sets one property, quoting
.I value
as
.IR rc (1)
does
.RB ( %q ).
.PP
.I Uievent
waits for the next event and fills
.IR e :
.IP
.EX
typedef struct Uievent {
	char	*kind;	/* click text enter check slide close */
	char	*id;	/* the node; nil for close */
	char	*arg;	/* the rest of the line, or "" */
	char	line[1024];
} Uievent;
.EE
.PP
The strings point into
.BR e->line ,
good until the next call.
It returns \-1 when
.I ui
is gone.
.PP
.I Uiclose
closes the files and unmounts them; the window stays until
.I ui
ends.
.SH EXAMPLE
A button that counts its clicks:
.IP
.EX
Ui *u;
Uievent e;
int n;

if((u = uinew("count", nil)) == nil)
	sysfatal("uinew: %r");
uictl(u, "new l label\enset l text 0\ennew b button\enset b text add one\en");
n = 0;
while(uievent(u, &e) >= 0 && strcmp(e.kind, "close") != 0)
	if(strcmp(e.kind, "click") == 0 && strcmp(e.id, "b") == 0)
		uictl(u, "set l text %d", ++n);
uiclose(u);
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/libui
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ui (4),
.IR rio (1)
.SH BUGS
A line of
.B event
longer than
.B e->line
is cut.
